## What I built
- **`apps/tools/gen-parity-manifest.ts`** ΓÇö AST-based generator (TypeScript compiler API, loaded from `web/node_modules` via `createRequire` so no new deps). Scans `web/src`:
  - **Router** (`App.tsx`): `lazy(import)` map + nested `<Route>` tree ΓåÆ routeΓåÆpage resolution.
  - **Pages**: one `page` unit per page-component file. Per page it AST-collects panels (GlassPanel/ChartContainer/Card/StatCard/MetricCard), charts, maps, called hooks, i18n `t()` keys, and data states.
  - **HooksΓåÆendpoints**: parses each `use*.ts`, reconstructs `request('/path')` (template substitutions ΓåÆ `{expr}`), captures HTTP method + query params.
  - Validates **every unit against `manifest.schema.json`** (ajv), emits sorted/stable JSON, and has a `--check` drift mode (exit 1 on drift ΓÇö verified both directions).
- **`apps/tools/gen-parity-manifest.ps1`** ΓÇö runner (`-Check`, `-Gate`).
- **`apps/parity/parity-manifest.json`** ΓÇö 1754 units: 153 page, 148 route, 844 panel, 154 chart, 24 map, 282 api, 149 string-group.

